row(31, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'A THOUSAND TO A TRIBE, A THOUSAND TO A TRIBE, FOR ALL THE TRIBES OF ISRAEL — THE DOUBLED NUMERAL THE PARSER READS AS TWO, THE INK OF 31:5 SUMS TO TWELVE THOUSAND; R. YISHMAEL\'S 24,000 AGAINST R. AKIVA\'S 12,000 AND LEVI. {HP(31, 4, (("אלף", "למטה", "אלף", "למטה"), "A THOUSAND TO A TRIBE, A THOUSAND TO A TRIBE — the doubled phrase\'s one seat; the parser reads the doubling as two thousands [1000, 1000] (the distributive rule); 31:5 states the product, twelve thousand; the Sifrei 157:3: 24,000 (R. Yishmael — the doubling twice) against 12,000 (R. Akiva); the English drops the first name and reverses the second\'s arm"), (("לכל", "מטות", "ישראל", "תשלחו", "לצבא"), "for ALL THE TRIBES OF ISRAEL you shall send to the host — the phrase here and Joshua 22:14 (computed); the Sifrei: to INCLUDE the tribe of Levi (the Hebrew) — \'to exclude\' (the English)"))} → {AP(31, 4, (("אלפא", "לשבטא", "אלפא", "לשבטא"), "a thousand to a tribe, a thousand to a tribe"), (("לכל", "שבטיא", "דישראל", "תשלחון", "לחילא"), "for all the tribes of Israel you shall send to the host"))}. No narrative verb.')
